{"id": "xkosovo", "name": "Sharr Mountains National Park", "short": "Sharr Mountains", "place": "Kosovo", "lat": 42.2, "lon": 21.0, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Kosovo", "blurb": "Beech and pine forests, high pastures and the last Balkan lynx.", "tip": {"id": "wolf", "title": "Remove the wolves", "text": "Wolves hunt deer, chamois, boar and voles. Set Gray wolf to -100% and watch the herbivores grow, then the forest and pasture plants they eat."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Sharr Mountains National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharr_Mountains_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Sar Mountains", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0ar_Mountains"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Balkan lynx", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balkan_lynx"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Chamois", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balkan_chamois"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Griffon vulture", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Griffon_vulture"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Sharr Mountains National Park", "icon": "whitebark", "tier": "overview", "park": true, "kind": "Polar & mountain", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "Summer light drives growth in the meadows and forests, but the growing season is short at altitude."}, {"id": "snow", "sp": "snowpack and snowmelt", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "rainfall", "xh": 0.46, "desc": "Mountain rain and cloud water feed the forests and the high pastures."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "mountain soil", "xh": 0.66, "desc": "Forest and meadow soils hold the nutrients that plants take up."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "Break down fallen leaves, dead wood and carcasses, returning nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus sylvatica", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "A broadleaf tree of the lower and middle forest slopes. Its nuts and leaves feed many forest animals."}, {"id": "pine", "sp": "pinus peuce", "xh": 0.38, "wiki": "Macedonian pine", "desc": "A Balkan pine found in the upper forest belt of the Sharr range; its seeds and needles feed forest animals."}, {"id": "fescue", "sp": "festuca", "xh": 0.62, "name": "Mountain grasses", "desc": "Fescue grasses form part of the high pastures above the tree line, which are among the largest compact pastures in Europe."}, {"id": "gentian", "sp": "gentiana verna", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "chamois", "sp": "rupicapra rupicapra", "xh": 0.06, "name": "Balkan chamois", "wiki": "Balkan chamois", "desc": "A goat-antelope of steep rocky slopes. It grazes grasses and herbs in summer and eats conifer bark and needles in winter."}, {"id": "roe", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "A small forest deer that browses in the woods and meadow edges of the range."}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.34, "name": "Wild boar", "desc": "An omnivore of the forest that roots for nuts, plants and invertebrates."}, {"id": "hare", "sp": "lepus europaeus", "xh": 0.48, "desc": "A grass and herb eater of open ground; the Balkan lynx is known to hunt it."}, {"id": "squirrel", "sp": "sciurus vulgaris", "xh": 0.62, "name": "Eurasian red squirrel", "desc": "A tree squirrel of the conifer and mixed forests, feeding on seeds and nuts."}, {"id": "bankvole", "sp": "myodes glareolus", "xh": 0.76, "desc": "A small forest rodent eating seeds, fruit and green plants; a common prey of many predators."}, {"id": "snowvole", "sp": "dinaromys bogdanovi", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "A rare rock-dwelling rodent of Balkan mountains, recorded on the Sharr slopes."}, {"id": "marten", "sp": "martes foina", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "A flexible hunter and fruit eater that takes rodents, birds and eggs.", "ic": "fox"}, {"id": "badger", "sp": "meles meles", "xh": 0.38, "desc": "